##) SYNOPSIS:
==nmvn== **\<command-options\>**
manage multi-project maven worksets and versions

==nmvn== [**build**] {{maven-args...}}
==nmvn== **workset** [**list**|**path**|**get**|**set**|**add-root**|**remove-root**|**root**|**scan**|**edit**] [{{options...}}]
==nmvn== **version scan**    [{{scan-options}}] [**-j**|**--json**]
==nmvn== **version bump**    [{{scan-options}}] [**--dry**] [**--patch**|**--minor**|**--major**] [**--all**] [**--force**] [**--cascade**=<versions|references|none>] [**-a**] <GA[#VER]>...
==nmvn== **version update**  [{{scan-options}}] [**--dry**] [**--cascade**=<versions|references|none>] [**-a**] <GA#VER>...
==nmvn== **version release** [{{scan-options}}] [**--dry**] [**--strict**] [**-a** <GA#VER>]...
==nmvn== **version check**   [{{scan-options}}] [**--fail-on-warning**] [**-j**|**--json**]
==nmvn== **clean**           [**--simple**|**--gitignore**] [**--workset** <NAME|FILE>] [**--root** <DIR>]... [**--exclude** <GLOB>]... [**--no-ignore**]
==nmvn== **get**             <G:A:V> [<REPO>]
==nmvn== **diff-jar**        [**-r** <REPO_URL>]... <JAR1> <JAR2>

    {{scan-options}}: [**-w**|**--workset** <NAME|FILE>] [**-r**|**--root** <DIR>]... [**--exclude** <GLOB>]... [**--no-ignore**]

##) OPTIONS:

    ```sh -w <NAME|FILE> | --workset <NAME|FILE> | --config <NAME|FILE>```
        workset to use. Without it: ./workset.tson, ./nmvn.tson, ./.nmvn/config.tson,
        then the global workset.tson/nmvn.tson; with none of them the current directory is scanned.

    ```sh -r <DIR> | --root <DIR>```
        scan this directory instead of the workset roots. Can be specified multiple times.

    ```sh --exclude <GLOB>```
        skip matching paths (e.g. `**/generated/**`). Can be specified multiple times.

    ```sh --no-ignore```
        disable implicit generated-directory and `.gitignore` filtering for scan-based commands.
        Explicit `--exclude` patterns remain active.

    ```sh --gitignore | --fix-gitignore```
        in `clean` mode, check each scanned project's `target/` directory. When it is not
        excluded, append `target/` to that repository's `.gitignore` and untrack tracked
        target files with `git rm -r --cached`. Working-tree files are kept. With `--dry`
        only report what would change. This mode does not run Maven or delete `target/`.

    ```sh -a <GA[#VER]> | -a=<GA[#VER]> | --artifact=<GA[#VER]>```
        specify target artifact and optional version using standard Nuts '#' delimiter (e.g. `com.example:mod1#1.0.0.0`) or '=' delimiter (`com.example:mod1=1.0.0.0`). For bump, omitting version auto-increments using the selected or default policy. Can be specified multiple times.

    ```sh -p | --patch | -m | --minor | -M | --major```
        increment explicitly selected target artifacts by patch, minor, or major.
        Use `--all` to deliberately target every artifact in the workset.

    ```sh --all```
        explicitly select every workspace artifact for `version bump`. Without this flag,
        at least one artifact coordinate (or a configured bump instruction) is required.

    ```sh --force```
        in bump mode, force advancing an artifact that is already in snapshot mode. This is the standard nuts session option (long form only; `-f` is `--fetch`), handled by the nuts session like `--dry`.

    ```sh -c=<mode> | --cascade=<mode>```
        control downstream cascading behavior (`versions`, `references`, or `none`). Use the `=` form.
        - `versions` (or `--cascade-versions`): update references AND bump dependent module versions.
        - `references` (or `--cascade-references-only`, `--no-cascade-versions`): update references in dependent POMs, but leave their project versions untouched.
        - `none` (or `--no-cascade`): touch only the target artifact's POM; leave downstream POMs completely untouched.
        - Default: `references` (cascade-references-only); dependent project versions are not bumped.

    ```sh --dry | -D```
        preview unified diff of changes without modifying files on disk. Default is non-dry (applies changes).

    ```sh --strict```
        in release mode, fail if any unmanaged external snapshot dependency is detected.

    In release mode, `-a <GA#VER>` only overrides the release version of that artifact:
    every -SNAPSHOT artifact in the scanned roots is still released. Narrow the scan with
    `--root`/`--exclude` to release a subset.

    ```sh -j | --json```
        output machine-readable JSON for CI/CD pipelines.

    ```sh --fail-on-warning```
        in check mode, fail with exit code 1 if any warnings are detected.

##) WORKFLOWS:

    **1. Start New Development Cycle (Post-Release Bump with Cascading Versions)**
    Bump released module `A` to snapshot and cascade to dependent modules `B`:
    ```sh nmvn version bump -a com.example:A --patch --cascade-versions --dry```
    ```sh nmvn version bump -a com.example:A --patch --cascade-versions```

    **2. Active Development Bump (Auto-Increment / Idempotent)**
    Bump module using semver flags without needing to calculate next version:
    ```sh nmvn version bump -a com.example:A --minor```
    ```sh nmvn version bump -a com.example:A --patch --force```

    **3. Strict Version Assignment / Dependency Alignment (`update`)**
    Update artifact to a strict version and align all references across workspace:
    ```sh nmvn version update -a net.thevpc.hl:hadra-lang#0.1.1```
    ```sh nmvn version update -a com.example:core#2.0.0-SNAPSHOT```

    **4. Synchronized / Lockstep Monorepo Bump**
    Bump all workspace modules together:
    ```sh nmvn version bump --all --minor --dry```
    ```sh nmvn version bump --all --minor```
    ```sh nmvn version bump -a com.example:core#2.0.0-SNAPSHOT -a com.example:client#2.0.0-SNAPSHOT```

    **5. Upstream Parent or BOM Upgrade**
    Update shared parent POM or BOM across child modules:
    ```sh nmvn version update -a com.example:company-parent#5.0.0```

    **6. Release Artifacts (Fix Snapshots)**
    Strip -SNAPSHOT from all workspace artifacts and convert references to release:
    ```sh nmvn version release --dry```
    ```sh nmvn version release --strict```
    Release everything, but pick explicit versions for some artifacts:
    ```sh nmvn version release -a com.example:core#1.0.0 -a com.example:client#1.0.0```

##) EXAMPLES:

```sh nmvn install -DskipTests```
   run maven install with the embedded maven

```sh nmvn build clean install```
   maven clean install (`build` is needed because `clean` alone is nmvn's own command)

```sh nmvn clean --simple```
   delete the target/ folder of every scanned project

```sh nmvn clean --gitignore --dry```
   report projects whose target/ is not ignored or is still tracked by Git

```sh nmvn clean --gitignore```
   add target/ to each repository .gitignore and untrack it (keeps files on disk)

```sh nmvn workset add-root ../other-project --scan```
   add a root folder to current workset and scan discovered artifacts

```sh nmvn workset remove-root ../other-project --scan```
   remove a root folder from current workset and rescan

```sh nmvn workset list --recent```
   list recent worksets

```sh nmvn version scan```
   scan and print multi-project dependency graph

```sh nmvn version check```
   audit workspace for version discrepancies, mixed snapshot/releases, and cycles
